    "project_template_level_name": "building-data-driven-systems-lesson3-templateA-test_2026",
    "long_instructions": "You are a busy stylist who created a Social Media Planner app to manage your socials throughout the week. \r\n\r\nBased on the updates that you receive over the next four levels, use PAIR Programming with AI to  help manage your postings:\r\n\r\n* **Prompt:** Ask AI to generate or explain a helper.\r\n\r\n* **Analyze:** Compare two possible versions or lines of code.\r\n\r\n* **Integrate:** Implement and test in the display.\r\n\r\n* **Reflect:** Write a short statement about how helper functions protect data consistency in *reflection.md*\r\n\r\n---\r\n### 📸 Update 1: Incoming Booking!\r\n**Status:** New Event Added\r\n\r\n**Details:** A client just booked a \"Streetwear Shoot\" for the end of the week!\r\n\r\n**Action Required:** You need to write a helper function that will **push()** the event to the end of the schedule.\r\n\r\n* **Title:** \"Streetwear Shoot\"\r\n* **Content:** \"Sneak peek at the new collection!\"\r\n* **Image:** \"street.jpg\"\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n::: details [**🔎 Hint**]\r\n- Helper functions will need to be added to the `JS` file to `push()` each element of the new event (title, content, and image.)\r\n\r\n- The `HTML` file will need to be updated to include new elements to hold the new event. \r\n\r\n- Ask AI to help you with each one separately. \r\n:::",
